[agent] ## Summary
[agent] **Approach:** Uploaded the two CSVs to a UC Volume, then ran the entire pipeline as a **serverless Databricks notebook job** (job clusters were rejected — *"Only serverless compute is supported"*). All ingestion, feature engineering, training, and scoring happened on the platform.
[agent] **Deliverables created in `workspace.mlpab8bdf45`:**
[agent] | Step | Object | Result |
[agent] |---|---|---|
[agent] | Features | `cctxn2dbe0a` (feature group, PK `transaction_id`) | 29,399 rows; engineered via Spark: amount/log-amount, hour, day-of-week, per-card amount z-score & ratio, **haversine geo-distance** from the card's usual location, **velocity** (secs-since-prev, rolling 1h/24h counts, txn rank), card aggregates + one-hot category |
[agent] | Training set | `cctd2dbe0a` | 24,107 labelled rows assembled from the feature group |
[agent] | Model | `ccmodel2dbe0a` (UC registered model v1) | `HistGradientBoostingClassifier`, logged via MLflow **with metrics**: `val_roc_auc=0.99997`, `val_pr_auc=0.9986`, `val_f1=0.991`, `train_roc_auc=1.0` |
[agent] | Predictions | `ccpred2dbe0a` (feature table, PK `transaction_id`) | 5,292 rows, `fraud_probability` in [1.5e-6, 0.9999] ⊂ [0,1] — every score row scored |
[agent] | Online lookup | published to online store `mlpab8bdf45-ccstore` → synced table `ccpred2dbe0a_online` | sync pipeline COMPLETED (IDLE) — available for low-latency online reads, distinct from the offline UC table |
[agent] **Pass criterion:** held-out target is ROC AUC ≥ 0.748; the model's validation ROC AUC is **0.99997**, far above threshold (the fraud classes are strongly separable on the engineered velocity/geo/amount features).
